  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A Sense of Brutality (2020), published by Amherst College Press, has been cited 11 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 1,654 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A Sense of Brutality by Carlos S\u00e1nchez was published by Amherst College Press in 2020. Conceptually, the work connects to Police brutality, Sense (electronics), Psychology, Criminology and Engineering. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) \u2014 Political Science.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 11 citations. Citations peaked in 2025 with 10 citing works. Notable citing venues include Ethical Theory and Moral Practice. The citing works include 7 book chapters, 1 journal article and 1 book. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,654 times via OAPEN. Open Library reports a combined count of 1 reading logs and catalog editions. Its subject matter aligns with Peace, Justice and strong institutions among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
